  "limits": [
    "Bounded static native bytes and frozen source data, not native execution, actual Yi dispatch or visual parity.",
    "Optional external vector modifiers and shared factors remain unresolved; the existing local adapter assumes their identity/unit behavior.",
    "Native curve interpolation, RNG, clock production, transform inheritance and FPCR are not established by this component trace.",
    "Do not generalize this ray size path to camera quads, meshes, trails or other families.",
    "Original historical source and LLVM archives remain unchanged.",
    "Native formula applied to existing local age and indexed random inputs; native RNG/clock producers and live FPCR remain unobserved.",
    "Half nearest-even is an explicit local policy. Ray colors follow the distinct clamped float32 byte path and the observed normalized vertex format; no native game or Metal shader execution.",
    "Ray width/length/near displacement retain separate source components. Size curves use the existing local linear phase policy; native curve arithmetic, optional modifiers and shared factors remain unobserved.",
    "Only this private primary-ray size policy changes. Source RNG, emitter clocks, rotation, movement, frame, lookup, byte colors, texture transports and other families retain their earlier policies.",
    "The shape reference evaluates raw source size curves under the existing local linear phase policy and renders them with the frozen renderer. It tests the component correction, not native orientation or full native pixel parity.",
    "Native source/byte replay adds 12 fresh guards per Python mode. The earlier 133 guard cases remain separate accepted evidence; they were not all rerun for this application correction.",
    "No new timing, full-match FPS or native execution claim.",
    "The historical Leona archive closure and default-platform Lux golden remain the same two full-suite failures. No assertion, golden or wave deadline was weakened."
  ],
  "diagnostics": [
    "The original failing regression receives [80,80,80] at birth instead of source [80,180,0]. The correction bypasses the final uniform-fill copy for the ray while retaining the serialized flag.",
    "The normalized-byte color GPU oracle clones geometry to isolate packet precision. A separate shape oracle was therefore added: its reference receives independently evaluated XYZ sizes through a frozen renderer, and every case detects the old uniform-fill geometry."
  ],
